Base model
----------

This model is a modified version of the tessdata_best Hebrew model
(heb.traineddata) of the Tesseract OCR project,
https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tessdata_best, commit
e12c65a915945e4c28e237a9b52bc4a8f39a0cec, sha256
dbaa827aea6bc21215638447f17783a1004987c2d0bf5573d111fee397abdae5, licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

HeOCR modified it on 2026-11-09: its LSTM network was fine-tuned with
Tesseract's lstmtraining on real scanned Hebrew lines, and two characters
were added to its character set (the maqaf U+05BE and the en dash U+2013).
Its dictionary components were rebuilt from the base model's own word list
with build files from https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/langdata_lstm, commit
07930fd9f246622c26eb5de794d9212ceac432d3, licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0.

Software
--------

The model was trained with, and runs in, Tesseract 5.5.3
(https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tesseract), licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. The model file contains no Tesseract code.

Training data: scans
--------------------

From the collections of the National Library of Israel / מאוסף הספרייה הלאומית

The training lines were cut from these National Library of Israel (NLI)
scans. Each record's IIIF manifest carries NLI's licence "public domain,
free use"
(https://www.nli.org.il/contenteditors/pages-for-terms-of-use/public-domain-free-use)
and the attribution "מאוסף הספרייה הלאומית". They were fetched from NLI's
IIIF service (https://iiif.nli.org.il/IIIFv21/<record>/manifest), the
route HeOCR's legal strategy calls nli_free_use. None is a Google-digitized
"public domain, non-commercial use" scan.

  NLI record 990020308000205171: Yeshayahu Berashadsky (1871-1908), Ketavim
    Aharonim, with a biography by Pesach Kaplan (1870-1943) and an essay by
    Ben-Avigdor (1866-1921). Warsaw: Tushiya, 1910. 6,076 lines.
  NLI record 990020495520205171: Shmuel Leib Citron (1860-1930), Me-Ahorei
    ha-Pargod. Vilna: Z. Matz, 1923-1925. 6,052 lines.
  NLI record 990020522850205171: Shmuel Tchernowitz (1879-1929), Im Shahar.
    Jerusalem: Ha-Madpis, 1927. 1,511 lines.
  NLI record 990019385920205171: Azriel Natan Frank (1863-1924), Sefer
    Agadot ha-Zohar. Warsaw: Ahiasaf, 1923-1924. 8 lines.
  NLI record 990013538860205171: Yitzhak Katzenelson (1885-1944), Shirim.
    Lodz: Hovevei Shira, 1938. 1 line.

Checkpoint selection used lines from two further NLI "public domain, free
use" scans, fetched the same way. They were not trained on:

  NLI record 990020250940205171: Kadish Yehuda Silman (1880-1937),
    Sansinim. Jerusalem and Tel Aviv: Tarbut, 1929.
  NLI record 990018546440205171: Reuven Brainin (1862-1939), Avraham Mapu:
    Hayav u-Sfarav. Vilna and Warsaw: Tushiya, 1928.

Every author, contributor and illustrator of these books died more than 70
years ago, so the books are in the public domain in Israel. The books
printed before 1931 are also past the United States copyright term. The US
status of Shirim (1938, one training line) is not established.

The model contains no scan images. The line crops are not distributed with
it.

Training data: text
-------------------

Each training line is labelled with the transcription of the same edition
from Project Ben-Yehuda (https://benyehuda.org), public domain dump release
2026-03 (https://github.com/projectbenyehuda/public_domain_dump). Its
licence states that the data files are in the public domain. Credit: Project
Ben-Yehuda volunteers.

Evaluation data (not used for training)
---------------------------------------

The model was scored on 38 page transcriptions from Hebrew Wikisource
(https://he.wikisource.org), licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike licence (CC BY-SA), as adjudicated by HeOCR's human
reviewers. They were used only to score the model after it was chosen,
never for training, tuning or checkpoint selection. The model contains no
Wikisource text.

